# One Component Per File

NEVER define multiple React components in the same file.

Each component MUST have its own dedicated file. Split aggressively into small, focused entities.

- Extract sub-components into separate files, even if they're small
- Colocate related components in the same folder if needed
- Prefer a flat component alongside its parent rather than inlining it

```
❌ BAD — components/SceneCard.tsx
export function SceneCard() { ... }
function SceneCardHeader() { ... }  // should be its own file
function SceneCardActions() { ... } // should be its own file

✅ GOOD — split into separate files
components/SceneCard.tsx        → SceneCard
components/SceneCardHeader.tsx  → SceneCardHeader
components/SceneCardActions.tsx → SceneCardActions
```
